                    {
                        "form_id": "e79f6b86-9a84-4ecf-aeeb-13039b4d6638",
                        "entry_id": "668a65e8-074b-3264-a037-06e3d90b4559",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "гяу́рах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f90bc97f-deda-3dd2-860c-281f9fb65821",
                        "entry_id": "668a65e8-074b-3264-a037-06e3d90b4559",
                        "glosses": [
                            "религ., пренебр. презрительное обозначение человека, не исповедующего ислам, любого немусульманина"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1876dcbc-d87a-40ff-9169-70f87d560a55",
                                "sense_id": "f90bc97f-deda-3dd2-860c-281f9fb65821",
                                "text": "Через несколько мгновений поднимаю их ― и вижу: мой Карагёз летит, развевая хвост, вольный как ветер, а гяуры далеко один за другим тянутся по степи на измученных конях."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "19b078de-4496-44dc-a3d5-703cbd844dc0",
                                "sense_id": "f90bc97f-deda-3dd2-860c-281f9fb65821",
                                "text": "― Может ли существовать какая-нибудь священная связь с гяурами?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c4db7ae-7e9c-4140-8993-f96d0a740fbc",
                                "sense_id": "f90bc97f-deda-3dd2-860c-281f9fb65821",
                                "text": "Удар кинжалом или пуля отплачивают казаку за мусульманскую кровь, пролитую неведомо каким гяуром, ― кто станет разбирать виноватого?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "59f458ec-297d-4b3d-83c7-f958d3957baf",
                        "source_entry_id": "668a65e8-074b-3264-a037-06e3d90b4559",
                        "source_sense_id": "f90bc97f-deda-3dd2-860c-281f9fb65821",
                        "target_lang_word": "giaour",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "giaour",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e00d2797-2b2e-396f-b2bc-b24e2d1fdc80",
                                        "entry_id": "72290b04-6d8a-3ac7-ad02-78567257a715",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A non-Muslim, especially a Christian, an infidel; especially as used by Turkish people with particular reference to Christians such as Greeks, Armenians, Bulgarians, Serbs and Assyrians."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slur"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c766cf6-4dc4-47de-ae87-cb90f56a67ee",
                                                "sense_id": "e00d2797-2b2e-396f-b2bc-b24e2d1fdc80",
                                                "text": "And far beyond the Moslem's power / Had wrong'd him with the faithless Giaour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f243fef-de98-4a65-8598-9d70a580cae4",
                                                "sense_id": "e00d2797-2b2e-396f-b2bc-b24e2d1fdc80",
                                                "text": "We men are not a race of freebooters or giaours; not when our argosies are prey and food to the evil fish-of-metal whose lair is a German U-boat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71d0c561-2f05-4dd5-a51b-95bc0f86b755",
                                                "sense_id": "e00d2797-2b2e-396f-b2bc-b24e2d1fdc80",
                                                "text": "I shudder in delight when I think of two-hundred-year-old books, dating back to the time of Tamerlane, volumes for which acquisitive giaours gleefully relinquish gold pieces and which they carry all the way back to their own countries[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecd4d5e4-5d48-43fe-8fa0-3015356e79e1",
                                                "sense_id": "e00d2797-2b2e-396f-b2bc-b24e2d1fdc80",
                                                "text": "Byron’s tale called The Giaour is supposed to be told by a Turkish fisherman who had been employed all the day in the gulf of Ægi’na, and landed his boat at night-fall on the Piræus, now called the harbor of Port Leonê.[…]The tale is this: Leilah, the beautiful concubine of the Caliph Hasson^([sic]), falls in love with a giaour, flees from the seraglio, is overtaken by an emir, put to death, and cast into the sea. The giaour cleaves Hassan’s skull, flees for his life, and becomes a monk."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e2fc6dd8-b21b-453e-97df-95754f392268",
                        "source_entry_id": "668a65e8-074b-3264-a037-06e3d90b4559",
                        "source_sense_id": "f90bc97f-deda-3dd2-860c-281f9fb65821",
                        "target_lang_word": "giaur",
                        "target_lang_code": "pl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "giaur",
                                "target_lang_code": "pl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1d84d1bd-c5a2-30c6-a2ad-2637ebdadad6",
                                        "entry_id": "1a309bdc-7e55-3be5-89b3-d433c66fc199",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "() muzułmańskie określenie innowiercy, szczególnie chrześcijanina"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "pejorative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e3e8bd9-ae7e-4796-a5de-988096ce8883",
                                                "sense_id": "1d84d1bd-c5a2-30c6-a2ad-2637ebdadad6",
                                                "text": "…korsarstwo u Maurów nie było wcale rzeczą hańbiącą, ale czynem bohaterskim, rycerskim. Więc sami nawet członkowie rodziny sułtańskiej wysyłali statki na chwytanie i łupienie giaurów"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18cd4984-094d-40fb-8bb0-5250193754b2",
                                                "sense_id": "1d84d1bd-c5a2-30c6-a2ad-2637ebdadad6",
                                                "text": "Ci prawdziwi synowie pustyni witali nas wszędzie z radością, i z wschodnią iście gościnnością przyjmowali w swych namiotach. Znają oni wszyscy Blunta, uważają go za swojego, a nienawidząc wszystkiego co angielskie, pokochali tego giaura, który sercem i duszą do nich przylgnął"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d309e5e9-0290-4bad-8d99-c94f917b59c3",
                        "source_entry_id": "668a65e8-074b-3264-a037-06e3d90b4559",
                        "source_sense_id": "f90bc97f-deda-3dd2-860c-281f9fb65821",
